opencc (1.4.1+ds1-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/patches/0009-setup.py-Handle-python-binding-instead-of-cmake.patch:
    Stop setting ext.runtime_library_dirs. It baked the build directory
    into the DT_RUNPATH of the python extension; deleting that entry with
    chrpath afterwards still left the build path string behind in .dynstr
    (lintian: file-references-package-build-path). Only -L is needed at
    link time, and the installed extension finds libopencc.so.1.4 through
    the regular linker search path.
  * debian/rules: Drop the now unneeded chrpath call, and set
    LD_LIBRARY_PATH for the pybuild test run so the freshly built
    libopencc is still picked up without an RPATH.
  * debian/control: Drop the chrpath build dependency accordingly.
  * debian/control: Let opencc suggests opencc-jieba package, and let
    opencc-jieba declare Enhances: opencc.

 -- Boyuan Yang <byang@debian.org>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:18:45 -0400

