opencc (1.4.1+ds1-1~exp1) experimental; urgency=medium

  * debian/control: Bump debhelper compat to v14.
  * debian/copyright: Updated.
  * debian/docs: Rename to libopencc-dev.docs.

  [ Frank Lin ]
  * New upstream release.
  * d/copyright: Stop excluding deps/darts-clone-*/*; upstream darts-
    clone fork now provides validate()/copy_array() used by
    src/DartsDict.cpp, which the separate system darts package (a
    different upstream) does not have.
  * d/rules: Disable USE_SYSTEM_DARTS accordingly; build against the
    now-shipped bundled darts-clone fork.
  * d/control: Drop no-longer-needed Build-Depends on darts.
  * d/patches: Refresh 0003, 0004, 0005, 0009 for the new upstream
    source tree.
  * d/patches: Add 0010-fix-git-version-fallback.patch; upstream
    cmake/GitVersion.cmake falls back to a hardcoded version when no
    .git is present (always true for our source tarball), and the
    fallback was left at 1.4.0 in the 1.4.1 release, causing opencc --
    version to report the wrong version.
  * d/patches: Add 0011-drop-python-cli-entry-point.patch; the pybuild
    install step was overwriting the compiled C++ /usr/bin/opencc with a
    python console_scripts wrapper lacking a python3 dependency.
  * Rename libopencc1.3 to libopencc1.4: upstream bumped
    OPENCC_ABI_VERSION to 1.4 (libopencc.so.1.4), so the binary package,
    .install and .symbols files are renamed to match, with
    Breaks/Replaces on libopencc1.3. The .symbols file is regenerated
    against the built library.
  * d/libopencc1.4.symbols: fix cross-architecture size_t/thunk mangling
    caught by Salsa CI on i386, using native (regex)/(c++) dpkg-
    gensymbols pattern tags.

 -- Boyuan Yang <byang@debian.org>  Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:53:16 -0400

